How about comp.archives ? It already exists and is useful.. :-)
It can tell you where to start looking. So much for the quick answer...

There are *two* problems here. The first is where to look to retrieve the
sources via ftp or an automated mailer. The second part of the problem
is knowing when you need to go looking for an update. If you already have
the latest version there is no reason to waste your time downloading a
"shar file" just to find out your stuff was already up-to-date.

I have been wanting to put together a list of the most current versions
of the various packages available on the net for a while but just never
got around to it.  So here goes...

	 ********** REQUEST FOR VERSION INFORMATION *********

I am making a request to the authors of software posted to the net, in
*any* of the groups. Please send me information as to the current status of
your software. The information supplied should, at a minimum, consist of

Package Name:   sample_package
Version Number: 1.0
Patch Level:    1.0
Author(s):      Joe Programer
Email:          joe@host

Feel free to send along any other information that you want. Information
about where you distribute or how to obtain the most current version
would be a great help.

I will be posting the list monthly to comp.source.d. This will give everyone
a place to look to see just what is the most current version/patchlevel of
software posted to the net.

Please send submissions and updates to:

	soft-request@ssbell.uu.net
		 or
	     kent@ssbell

I will also be making the list available via a mail server after the
initial posting.

